Sagan is an open source high performance, real-time log analysis
and correlation engine.  It is written in C and uses a multi-threaded
architecture to deliver high performance log and event analysis.

The Sagan structure and rules work similarly to the Suricata and Snort IDS
engines, which allows Sagan to correlate log events with these systems.
Sagan supports many output formats, log normalization via liblognorm,
GeoIP detection, script execution on events and automatic firewall support.

Sagan reads syslog-style events from a FIFO or a file and matches them
against Suricata/Snort-like rules, writing alerts to its own log, to
syslog or in Suricata EVE JSON format.
